            <h2 class="section-title">Our Signature Dish</h2>

            <section class="signature-card">
                <img src="/public/images/nasi lemak.png" alt="Nasi lemak plate">
                <div class="signature-copy">
                    <h3>Nasi Lemak - The National Dish</h3>
                    <div class="tag-row">
                        <span>&#11088; National Favourite</span>
                        <span>&#128681; Traditional Cuisine</span>
                    </div>
                    <p>Nasi lemak is widely regarded as Malaysia's national dish. The fragrant rice is cooked in coconut milk and pandan leaves, giving it a rich and aromatic flavor. It is traditionally served with spicy sambal, crispy fried anchovies, roasted peanuts, fresh cucumber slices, and a boiled egg.</p>
                    <p>Originally enjoyed as a simple breakfast among local communities, nasi lemak has evolved into an all-day favorite. Variations may include fried chicken, beef rendang, or seafood, making it both versatile and deeply rooted in Malaysia's culinary heritage.</p>
                    <div class="signature-ingredients">
                        <article>
                            <h4>Bahan Nasi Lemak:</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>500 gr Beras (dicuci bersih)</li>
                                <li>250 ml Santan kental</li>
                                <li>Air secukupnya (sesuai takaran masak nasi)</li>
                                <li>Daun pandan (ikat simpul)</li>
                                <li>Serai (geprek)</li>
                                <li>Jahe (iris tipis)</li>
                                <li>Garam secukupnya</li>
                            </ul>
                        </article>
                        <article>
                            <h4>Bahan Sambal:</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Bawang merah & bawang putih (dihaluskan)</li>
                                <li>Cabai merah besar & cabai keriting (dihaluskan)</li>
                                <li>Gula merah/gula jawa</li>
                                <li>Terasi</li>
                                <li>Asam jawa</li>
                                <li>Garam</li>
                            </ul>
                        </article>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

