            <section class="satay-block">
                <div class="signature-card satay-card">
                    <div class="signature-copy">
                        <h3>Satay Ayam - Grilled Perfection</h3>
                        <div class="tag-row">
                            <span>&#11088; Street Food City</span>
                            <span>&#128681; Popular Local Menu</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Satay ayam consists of marinated chicken pieces skewered and grilled over charcoal. It is usually served with rich peanut sauce, sliced cucumber, and rice cakes.</p>
                        <p>The smoky aroma and sweet savory glaze make satay one of Malaysia's most loved festive foods, especially during celebrations and evening gatherings.</p>
                        <div class="signature-ingredients">
                            <article>
                                <h4>Bahan Satay & Marinasi:</h4>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>500 g chicken thigh, diced</li>
                                    <li>2 tbsp coriander powder</li>
                                    <li>1 tsp turmeric powder</li>
                                    <li>2 cloves garlic, grated</li>
                                    <li>1 tbsp lemongrass paste</li>
                                    <li>1 tbsp brown sugar</li>
                                    <li>1 tsp salt and white pepper</li>
                                    <li>2 tbsp cooking oil</li>
                                    <li>bamboo skewers</li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>
                            <article>
                                <h4>Bahan Bumbu Kacang Kental:</h4>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>200 g roasted peanuts</li>
                                    <li>3 red chilies (optional)</li>
                                    <li>2 shallots and garlic</li>
                                    <li>1 tbsp tamarind juice</li>
                                    <li>2 tbsp palm sugar</li>
                                    <li>1 cup water</li>
                                    <li>salt to taste</li>
                                </ul>
                            </article>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <img src="/public/images/satay ayam.png" alt="Satay ayam skewers">
                </div>
            </section>

            <h2 class="section-title beverage-title">Traditional Beverage</h2>

            <section class="beverage-section">
                <div class="beverage-card">
                    <div class="beverage-image">
                        <img src="/public/images/teh tarik.jpeg" alt="Teh tarik glass">
                    </div>
                    <div class="beverage-copy">
                        <h3>Teh Tarik - Malaysia's Signature Drink</h3>
                        <div class="tag-row">
                            <span>Traditional Beverage</span>
                            <span>Social Culture</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Teh tarik, literally meaning \"pulled tea,\" is a beloved Malaysian beverage made from strong black tea and condensed milk. The tea is poured back and forth between two containers to create a frothy texture and smooth consistency.</p>
                        <p>Commonly found in local coffeehouses or \"mamak\" stalls, teh tarik represents Malaysia's vibrant social culture. It is often enjoyed during casual conversation and late-night gatherings.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="beverage-details">
                    <div class="beverage-ingredients">
                        <h4>Ingredients for Teh Tarik :</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>2 black tea bags</li>
                            <li>200 ml hot water</li>
                            <li>2 - 3 tablespoons condensed milk</li>
                            <li>100 ml evaporated milk (optional)</li>
                            <li>Sugar to taste (optional)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

